        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12354849/comment/12447786",
          "id": "12447786",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=ianeboston",
            "name": "ianeboston",
            "key": "ianeboston",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10453",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10453",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10453",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10453"
            },
            "displayName": "Ian Boston",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/London"
          },
          "body": "Question.\n\nDoes this feature include the situation where there are 3 or more nodes all writing to Jackrabbit.... or is it the use case where there is one master jackrabbit and a number of slave (read-only) jackrabbits ?\n\nMy understnading of JCR-169 was that it was asking for the former (is all writable).... but not a problem if this wont address that aspect.\n\nThanks",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=ianeboston",
            "name": "ianeboston",
            "key": "ianeboston",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10453",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10453",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10453",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10453"
            },
            "displayName": "Ian Boston",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/London"
          },
          "created": "2006-11-07T13:29:56.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-11-07T13:29:56.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12354849/comment/12448517",
          "id": "12448517",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=pankaj.gupta",
            "name": "pankaj.gupta",
            "key": "pankaj.gupta",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Pankaj Gupta",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Thanks for geting started on this issue. Its a high priority one for us and perhaps many other Jackrabbit users.\n\nCouple of questions:\n1) Is the search index in other clusters also synced up if each cluster has the index in its local disk? Or is it required to have the search index  in a common file system?\n2) Are the other clusters updated immediately? For example, if one cluster adds a new node, is it immediately visible to other sessions in other clusters, as is mandated by the JCR spec?\n\nThanks\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=pankaj.gupta",
            "name": "pankaj.gupta",
            "key": "pankaj.gupta",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Pankaj Gupta",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2006-11-09T16:47:18.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-11-09T16:47:18.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12354849/comment/12448792",
          "id": "12448792",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dpfister",
            "name": "dpfister",
            "key": "dpfister",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Dominique Pfister",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "I quickly gained the impression, that creating a file for every journal record could lead to serious problems because file systems are usually not very good in handling a lot of entries. I therefore changed the default file-based journal implementation to append records to one file until its size has passed some limit. Verified that this works\n\nFixed in revision 473383.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dpfister",
            "name": "dpfister",
            "key": "dpfister",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Dominique Pfister",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2006-11-10T16:33:04.000+0000",
          "updated": "2006-11-10T16:33:04.000+0000"
        },
        {
